# Core APP Generic Installation Wizard

Task: `AIPIFY.CORE.APP.GENERIC.INSTALLATION.WIZARD.V1`

## Ownership

- **Core** owns the authoritative `installation_contract` on `app_portal_integration_providers`.
- **Customer APP** only renders the generic `InstallationWizard` from the canonical Core contract.
- Platform Admin configures the contract; APP never invents provider-specific wizards.

## Hard rules

1. No provider-specific wizard components.
2. No customer-specific wizard components (including UnoNight special-cases).
3. No parallel provider registry — extend the existing provider row.
4. Minimize customer technical effort; assistance-first UX is mandatory.
5. Prefer Aipify-managed / guided over self-service when supported.
6. Dynamic global locale list from Core language foundation (`LOCALES`) — never hardcode locale tabs/unions in the wizard.
7. English fallback required; never show raw translation keys to customers.
8. Role-based presentation from the same contract (customer vs internal).
9. No raw technical/internal copy to customer audiences.
10. No activation before verified; no auto-activation from wizard completion alone.
11. No secret plaintext to client, logs, or session `field_values`.
12. Pause/resume required; session state is server-authoritative.
13. State transitions validated in Core RPCs — client cannot invent authority.
14. Reference fixtures are not live Production providers.
15. Premium, responsive, dark-mode, and accessibility requirements apply.
16. Authenticated Production proof is required before `PRODUCTION_READY`.
17. Connected integrations support safe read-only wizard preview via the same generic `InstallationWizard` renderer (`mode: "preview"`).
18. Preview must never create or mutate installation sessions, call test/verify/activate/save/invite, or read secret plaintext.
19. Support mode switching in preview is local UI state only and resets on close.
20. Preview is tenant-bound and requires integration manage authorization (`can_manage`).
21. Dynamic locale remains required for preview copy — no hardcoded locale lists.

